1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,631
It's finally here.

2
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:08,842
Midori's first love.

3
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:09,801
Could it be…

4
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:13,304
you have come to dislike us?

5
00:00:13,388 --> 00:00:16,975
But Midori is completely
unused to romance.

6
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:18,309
I…

7
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:20,020
Mr. Nishigami…

8
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:21,855
A typhoon is coming soon.

9
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:25,316
Those five you are
so close with will all die.

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,987
Your recent actions
have been unacceptable.

11
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,990
You haven't forgotten
your mission, have you?

12
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:35,577
You taught us many things and helped us.

13
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:39,164
So we've had a fun and safe vacation.

14
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,373
Three.

15
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:41,291
Two.

16
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,208
One.

17
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,712
Thank you for always protecting the villa.

18
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:56,973
Typhoon No.13 is expected
to maintain its extreme intensity,

19
00:00:57,057 --> 00:01:00,351
and make landfall
in the Kanto region late tonight.

20
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,103
The typhoon scares me!

21
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,981
This typhoon is quite strong, huh.

22
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,442
It will probably miss us.
It's always like that.

23
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:09,527
The news is just trying to scare us.

24
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:10,570
That's true.

25
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:14,240
You think work might be canceled tomorrow,
but then you wake up, and it's sunny.

26
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,993
Looks like it will rain
quite a bit this time.

27
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,329
I don't think I can fish in this weather.

28
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,082
Then, what can we do indoors?

29
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:23,917
Okay!

30
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,252
Tonight, let's hold one of these!

31
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,004
-Huh?
-What?

32
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:30,089
-What is "these"?
-Here goes.

33
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:33,551
What is it?

34
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:36,805
Shut up!

35
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:40,850
-We will hold a card tournament!
-Huh?

36
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,352
In this day and age?

37
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:44,521
Why not? I found these cards here.

38
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,606
-I wonder if Grandma used them?
-They're big.

39
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:49,234
-They are, right?
-What game should we play?

40
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:50,693
-They're huge!
-Old Maid!

41
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:52,904
-Old Maid using Grandma's cards!
-So big!

42
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:55,115
-The heck is that?
-Stop it!

43
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,241
This is the Old Maid card.

44
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:58,159
I drew an old maid!

45
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,911
Grandma, I'm sorry!

46
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:00,870
Here.

47
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,247
-You don't have it?
-Pick whichever.

48
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:04,833
-You don't have it, right? Okay.
-Nope, I don't.

49
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:07,836
Okay! Huh, what is this? Can I pick?

50
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:10,004
-Will Mr. Nishigami come?
-Oh, sorry!

51
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:14,259
He may be busy preparing for the typhoon.

52
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,176
Right.

53
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:17,614
Looks like a fun time, huh?

54
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:18,740
A barbecue?

55
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,033
JAPAN DIVISION HEAD
LADY YOMI

56
00:03:20,116 --> 00:03:21,409
Nice to be young.

57
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:25,663
Sorry for calling you here so suddenly.

58
00:03:26,831 --> 00:03:27,707
Now…

59
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:32,003
This is your final warning.

60
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:35,840
Tonight is the night.

61
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:41,012
Let me tell you what will happen
if you break the code.

62
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,807
Every human involved with you

63
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:48,353
will have all Grim Reaper
related memories erased.

64
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:51,940
In other words,
they will forget your very existence.

65
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:56,236
Every memory you shared this summer.

66
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:02,408
The feelings that girl has for you
will also disappear.

67
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,786
And of course,

68
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:09,916
you yourself will be punished
by the laws of the underworld.

69
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:14,420
Calm down.

70
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:17,548
It's just a difference of a few decades.

71
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:22,845
Those humans will just meet
their demise a bit earlier.

72
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,474
Do your job, as you have always done.

73
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:28,643
Don't forget.

74
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:31,020
You're a Grim Reaper.

75
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:37,485
Time flows differently
for us and for humans.

76
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,949
I understand.

77
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:25,742
No lying!

78
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,493
It's a real weak one!

79
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:28,911
A weak one.

80
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:30,163
How about mine?

81
00:05:37,336 --> 00:05:39,047
I wonder what it's supposed to be?

82
00:05:39,881 --> 00:05:43,301
Did you copy it from a manga
you liked back in grade school?

83
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:44,719
Hmm…

84
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:47,180
Doesn't this look like Mr. Nishigami?

85
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:48,681
Oh, really?

86
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:49,682
Yeah.

87
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:56,439
So he's been your dream guy
ever since you were a kid?

88
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:58,357
-Right?
-I wonder.

89
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:02,111
Is Mr. Nishigami not coming?

90
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,029
Yeah…

91
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:05,782
On a day like this,
shouldn't he come to check on us?

92
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:09,327
I guess he's busy with the typhoon,
since he's the caretaker here.

93
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:13,081
Oh, it's him!

94
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:14,332
What? Mr. Nishigami?

95
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:20,963
Mr. Nishigami.

96
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:42,860
Mr. Nishigami, please sit in the middle.

97
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,612
-Six cans!
-Okay!

98
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:46,447
Konta, another round of Old Maid?

99
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:48,199
I'm tired of Old Maid already!

100
00:06:48,282 --> 00:06:49,117
It's fine.

101
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,910
-Isn't there anything else?
-What?

102
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:53,287
I bet you haven't played cards
in a while either.

103
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:55,164
How long since your last game?

104
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,083
Still, I wonder if we'll be okay.

105
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:59,252
Is it always like this around here?

106
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:03,506
No, this typhoon
is an especially large one.

107
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,842
I'm sure it will be fine.

108
00:07:05,925 --> 00:07:07,969
It's not raining that much yet.

109
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:12,348
Will you have dinner with us today too?

110
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:15,893
But, Midori, do we still have food?
I don't think we can buy anything now.

111
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,563
True, feels like it will start raining
the moment we step outside.

112
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:22,150
Yeah. So today, with leftovers,
I'll make Napolitan pasta.

113
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:23,401
Oh, Napolitan!

114
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:26,154
We can't do a barbecue,
but I'll make a yummy napolitan.

115
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:27,071
Sure.

116
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,323
Mr. Nishigami,
you should just call it a day.

117
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:30,908
Yeah, that's right.

118
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,452
Let's drink.

119
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,954
-Here you go.
-Yeah!

120
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,039
Thank you.

121
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:38,207
What are we playing?

122
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,167
-Daifugo!
-Daifugo!

123
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:52,722
What?

124
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:01,647
Mr. Nishigami?

125
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:11,073
What?

126
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,409
Such a thing is impossible!

127
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:14,994
I mean,

128
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:20,541
the typhoon passes through multiple areas,
so I can't just divert it by myself.

129
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:21,501
It's beyond me.

130
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:24,921
Besides, such an urgent request?

131
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,173
A god on my level can't do it.

132
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:33,304
Don't look so scary! I can't do it!

133
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:37,308
You know if we try anything,
we will be punished, right?

134
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,228
Besides, what you want to stop
is the landslide, right?

135
00:08:40,311 --> 00:08:43,105
So, why not ask the Mountain God?

136
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:45,650
The Mountain God. Go ask them, yeah.

137
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:48,653
No one can stop that typhoon,
but the Mountain God…

138
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:51,155
The ground is within her control.

139
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:53,866
If you ask them,
they can do something. Okay?

140
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:54,867
Oh, he's gone.

141
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,827
Where did he go? Huh?

142
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:03,459
At this rate,
he will be punished, for sure.

143
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:09,757
What are you saying?

144
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,093
You're a Grim Reaper, aren't you?

145
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:17,431
Please stop the landslide
that is about to happen.

146
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:20,726
What are you saying?

147
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:24,313
Lady Yomi already warned you many times.

148
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:28,609
Don't interfere
with the destiny of humans.

149
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:32,572
-Yes.
-Listen up, Reaper.

150
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:35,533
Even if you violate
the laws of the underworld

151
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:39,912
and give up your existence to save them,

152
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:42,999
they'll die in a few decades anyway.

153
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,334
A few decades.

154
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,502
No.

155
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:49,255
Some of them might only have a few years.

156
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:51,924
For this past month,

157
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:56,762
I've been watching those humans
spending time at that villa.

158
00:09:57,763 --> 00:10:00,433
They don't work, they don't study.

159
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:04,270
They just idle away every day
playing around.

160
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:07,648
Even if you save them tonight,

161
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:15,031
their self-indulgent and meaningless life
will only be extended by a little bit.

162
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,159
I believe

163
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:24,498
that the time they spent at this villa
will pave the way for their future.

164
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:28,919
Besides, to them, it's a long time.

165
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:32,340
A few decades to them should be equivalent

166
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:34,675
to hundreds…

167
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,344
No.

168
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:40,806
Thousands of years for us.

169
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:49,357
You talk just like a human now!

170
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,108
You…

171
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:56,197
You'll be erased like sand
by Lady Yomi, you know.

172
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:58,783
Like sand…

173
00:11:04,288 --> 00:11:07,708
A Reaper like me will die…

174
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:13,881
It's strange.

175
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:17,176
Right now, for the first time,

176
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:21,013
I truly feel

177
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:24,308
like I'm alive.

178
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:34,485
Seriously!

179
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:38,823
A Grim Reaper, taken in by humans…

180
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:41,117
That's a first for me.

181
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,873
I, too,

182
00:11:49,291 --> 00:11:54,088
have been watching the humans
living in Tatsumi Town for a long time.

183
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:59,718
And while there are humans who fulfill
their lifespan, less than 100 years,

184
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:02,805
and meet death peacefully,

185
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:08,436
there are also those
who die young due to illness or accidents.

186
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,731
You…

187
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:16,986
want to extend the time
of those young people, don't you?

188
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:22,283
Even if you must offer
your own existence in exchange.

189
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,622
A Grim Reaper, breaking the code.

190
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:32,710
How interesting.

191
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:38,007
Up on that mountain,

192
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:41,510
there is an old shrine nobody visits.

193
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:43,929
Try going there.

194
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:50,561
All natural disasters around here
are governed by that shrine.

195
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:55,107
If you go there, you may be able…

196
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,402
to change something.

197
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:00,988
Not that I care.

198
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:05,910
Over here, the rain and wind from earlier
have temporarily stopped.

199
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:08,871
Could this be the calm before the storm?

200
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:11,540
However, the intensity of the typhoon
has not dropped.

201
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,959
Please do not let your guard down.

202
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:23,385
Where did he go?

203
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:19,733
A Grim Reaper in human form?

204
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,652
A Grim Reaper…

205
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:23,195
Are you here to collect me?

206
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:28,450
I'm sorry.

207
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:30,578
I can't die. Yeah.

208
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,914
Because I'm a god.

209
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:13,454
Japan is home to myriad gods.

210
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:16,206
I control all weather!

211
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,209
The venerable Dragon God!

212
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:22,379
Today, without a doubt,
a landslide will occur.

213
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,965
You cannot change that absolute fact.

214
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,300
Goodbye.

215
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,928
They're being blown away!

216
00:15:29,553 --> 00:15:31,305
It's dangerous to stay here.

217
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,392
Mr. Nishigami?

218
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:38,145
I have met you before.

219
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,940
Who are you?

220
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,150
It was the best vacation.

221
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:44,985
Thank you.

222
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:46,904
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
